# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Playwright + TypeScript end-to-end tests for the application.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+
- npm

## Install

```bash
npm install
npx playwright install --with-deps
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env with your real BASE_URL and credentials
```

## Run

```bash
npm test                 # all tests, headless
npm run test:headed      # headed mode
npm run test:ui          # interactive UI mode
npm run report           # open the last HTML report
```

## Project structure

```
pages/             Page Object Model — base classes and per-feature POMs
modals/            Shared modal POMs
tests/             Test specs, mirrors pages/ structure
api/               API helpers (resource classes, listeners)
data/              Static test data
tests/utility/     Common helpers + example test patterns (excluded from execution)
```

## Conventions

Read `AGENTS.md` at the project root for the full convention guide. Highlights:

- Test names: `{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNNNN: Description`
- Every test uses `test.step` with Gherkin Given/When/Then/Cleanup
- Locators: `getByTestId` first, then semantic role/label/placeholder
- Dates: `typeDateValue()` only — never `fill()` or `pressSequentially()` on date inputs
- Data cleanup: `try/finally` with `cleanupNeeded` flag
- Web-first assertions only: `await expect(locator).toXxx()`

## AI-driven test development

If you use Claude Code, the `pw-kit` plugin contains 14 skills that auto-activate when you edit POM/test files, plus 5 slash commands for guided workflows:

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/pw-kit:new-test` | Guided test creation from a ticket |
| `/pw-kit:fix-test` | Investigate and fix a failing test |
| `/pw-kit:pre-pr` | Pre-PR convention checklist |
| `/pw-kit:create-test-cases` | Generate Gherkin test cases from a dev ticket |
| `/pw-kit:init` | Scaffold a new project from these conventions |

